$l$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Today Vasya solved the following problem at the informatics lesson: given a string consisting of symbols \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the task is to find the length of its minimal unique substring. He has written a solution to this problem and wants to test it. He is asking you to help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$2$$$ positive integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$, such that $$$(n \\bmod 2) = (k \\bmod 2)$$$, where $$$(x \\bmod 2)$$$ is operation of taking remainder of $$$x$$$ by dividing on $$$2$$$. Find any string $$$s$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ symbols \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", such that the length of its minimal unique substring is equal to $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$, separated by spaces ($$$1 \\leq k \\leq n \\leq 100\\,000$$$, $$$(k \\bmod 2) = (n \\bmod 2)$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of symbols \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Minimal length of the unique substring of $$$s$$$ should be equal to $$$k$$$. You can find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" suitable string. It is guaranteed, that there exists at least one such string."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1111"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n01010"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1011011\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test, it's easy to see, that the only unique substring of string $$$s = $$$\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text